{
  "summary": "PyMicroglia now has one Cell grid interface for traces and installed Circadian Workbench single-trace analyses. Registry-driven analysis controls share cell selection, preprocessing, layout and export helpers. Existing CD68, RBM3 and CRY1 experimental grids remain linked. The grid also supports compatible overlays, independent stacked lanes, separate panels and raw/mean/processed/completed-fit layers. The fitted-component option shows every FFT-NLLS wave in overlay or independent lanes, with individually significant conditional tests in red and other components in grey. Native and trace views retain test evidence, fitted amplitudes and clock gaps.",
